{"objects":[{"id":"flow","instance":"instance--b96dad5f-c519-5a1f-a718-912ca4a86c02","objects":["attack-action--1","attack-action--2","attack-action--3","attack-action--4","attack-action--5","attack-condition--1","attack-condition--2","instance--763adce8-107c-58c1-9b65-18fefd501b17","software--2","instance--635badaf-7b0e-521e-9f70-281b427efdd7","instance--2abde38b-0e53-5744-9006-a43572d80b3b","instance--cd8e2e12-554c-5e0b-9908-bf5d0aaae299","instance--3536a568-610f-5570-bba9-6dfe97bc9c2e","instance--fe58d3c1-faa4-512f-a0c3-fa75b622e227","instance--ed6039fe-678b-5ae9-9576-73e6ea35b0c8","instance--a6618e5f-2d2d-55c4-9d60-5edfe63f3ef7","instance--b879673b-0c82-5a65-8ee4-4f18f90200fb","instance--7cc46cbd-beb8-54eb-aef6-32656d039f20","instance--e5e1f9aa-9fe9-5106-95bc-0f29bb985397","instance--0e0aefbc-132c-5535-9d21-08a6439d6b20","instance--4ab6d46b-073a-553f-aa40-3f34b1c5e134","instance--336d1884-e8ff-58c6-893d-836dcb3031ae","instance--399a759f-97f7-528c-90c7-de3363f46907"],"properties":[["name","Invisible PUA Unicode GitHub repository compromise campaign"],["description","Aikido report describing a campaign in which a threat actor pushed legitimate-looking commits to GitHub repositories, appended hidden Unicode PUA JavaScript that decoded to a script fetching and executing a payload via Solana, and potentially harvested credentials for reuse in other repositories."],["scope","campaign"],["author",[["name","Ilyas Makari"]]],["external_references",[["item-1",[["source_name","www.aikido.dev"],["url","https://www.aikido.dev/blog/the-return-of-the-invisible-threat-hidden-pua-unicode-hits-github-repositorties"]]]]]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--ad592d05-6969-5b51-98a8-1ad9b6aab896","120":"instance--5850a8f4-8241-5e73-9bf0-dcd376cd5025","150":"instance--0da1498f-3beb-5916-a249-e0410a4a81e4","180":"instance--d3632784-7391-5a29-83e2-edab51db56c6","210":"instance--8bc47ca5-ca73-5a04-a9ea-918608f10871","240":"instance--6546eef6-c5ad-516e-a417-89916e651648","270":"instance--244e5a69-f465-564e-9d2c-93d4da44fc57","30":"instance--6a1fca3c-fdb6-536a-bbea-61ac2349a700","300":"instance--043a5b44-2864-5565-abce-1909204e5485","330":"instance--e10eb918-2b0b-56f4-9c82-f345ce21276c","60":"instance--33a99d1b-dad8-51f6-be74-e1614db9151b","90":"instance--380c79e9-b1eb-547c-bf01-a011db1201c1"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--1","properties":[["name","Push spoofed legitimate-looking commits"],["description","several of his own GitHub repositories had been updated, by him, at least according to the commit history. The commits looked legitimate. They contained realistic feature updates, small refactors, and even bug fixes that matched the project\u2019s coding style and commit messages. Apart from one difference, the email of the committer was set to . But at the end of these commits, each one had a single, identical addition:"],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0003","technique":"T1098"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--4f4d03a8-4502-5010-997b-9943e254395b","120":"instance--cefe62ac-5b6e-5ead-84fc-b4c632913a73","150":"instance--4d07a740-2467-5b95-ac8d-4a2ee8edd11e","180":"instance--1205f03c-a457-5a0b-87ef-3bbb7aac110f","210":"instance--96e7dc6a-9f86-5f69-8d45-a566303cd4c0","240":"instance--66237af6-bb19-5a51-9fa2-cbc4a96186f5","270":"instance--836dfd42-b475-50ca-9acf-4f11bd32b89f","30":"instance--efe92997-cc5c-538a-90bc-c09ffb1379f4","300":"instance--9c4a24ae-1426-5cb5-9d7c-792e6dd325b7","330":"instance--06c6a74a-ca7d-5703-88ea-a06a0933d21a","60":"instance--5e4f84e5-56b7-5b8f-9bc3-b4d59d371123","90":"instance--019deb6a-bab3-57db-9a53-11e3564bf7a4"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--2","properties":[["name","Append hidden eval payload"],["description","what sticks out is the call, which is often used to execute code dynamically. Only the input to appears empty. However, the empty string passed to in is not empty at all. It contains invisible Unicode characters, hidden code encoded with Private Use Area symbols, just like in the previous npm and Open VSX incidents.\n\nThis time, however, the delivery is far more subtle. Everything has been collapsed into a single line, leaving almost no visual clue. The malicious code is tucked inside what looks like normal project activity, hidden within legitimate commits."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0005","technique":"T1027"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--0ce35aea-35a2-52ae-a67b-985306bdefe7","120":"instance--312639d5-e6d9-57b1-850d-28f0a1eac2f6","150":"instance--9551a25e-2558-512e-9894-dd64a8d662bf","180":"instance--403becce-e0ad-5dcd-bc14-7c00453907da","210":"instance--2305f501-2712-5ec6-9d4e-1371b011e937","240":"instance--cf1b8cf6-1cbd-5afb-b653-aa693889dab5","270":"instance--1d3dc59a-40a0-5670-aa3e-1304ff762003","30":"instance--77063d4f-503a-5e9b-b622-15aa2cc6a8e7","300":"instance--beaab67f-8a54-5982-8c5d-9d2ed2d42c9f","330":"instance--4d3274ff-ef14-5a53-99be-01575194a98e","60":"instance--4154a6bf-290b-5fce-a557-5dc0f3e700fb","90":"instance--2992bc0b-df57-54e5-a17b-03a964338c09"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--3","properties":[["name","Fetch and execute Solana-delivered payload"],["description","The decoded PUA characters lead to a script that appears very similar to the Open VSX samples, which suggests we are likely dealing with the same threat actor. The decoded script appears to use Solana as a delivery channel, fetching and executing a payload from the blockchain."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0011","technique":"T1105"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--0f6e4da7-a5f4-54d7-866f-3bc6e8bcb019","120":"instance--015254b5-0906-577e-b3e3-3899f837d118","150":"instance--f7af5b8c-330a-58d5-b0da-a3d5f0bc6ad0","180":"instance--9f27ab21-2382-567d-b022-74ad5a29bd08","210":"instance--d799eb0a-7600-5b1a-a298-c47a78ceae4b","240":"instance--911c2c52-5974-5e08-b0b6-a9084d57c6ee","270":"instance--286444b4-97a1-58cd-9ca3-cffa04a15351","30":"instance--92192c38-5143-50e0-8c39-a96ea86e32e2","300":"instance--82bb3de0-bea5-5651-a1de-583283258c6d","330":"instance--4f0945c8-f644-50ce-8796-fea52a29dda1","60":"instance--16c43a2d-7356-521d-a507-5922e2c3337b","90":"instance--abce5c62-339a-5ed5-a0b8-dd66136cfe2f"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--4","properties":[["name","Steal tokens and secrets"],["description","Based on the Open VSX incidents, those payloads have been capable of stealing tokens and other secrets."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0006","technique":"T1555"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--a469636c-0cb2-50b9-92f9-644c8aa98197","120":"instance--d57b3a21-e910-5879-8148-40165cea451a","150":"instance--58250ef4-5bb4-5bf3-b33e-89493bbb395d","180":"instance--3e769cf2-c1e5-5d2e-81d4-892f48ce4d86","210":"instance--f6499e41-749c-5d7f-9346-96c08d0d5dfd","240":"instance--d9dcdfc8-5f42-546a-803a-0efcd5d4cf91","270":"instance--c9afd0f6-97ce-57b2-9d60-3557b6214809","30":"instance--75f82155-f5ff-5619-8bf8-aae22937cab0","300":"instance--25e2d26e-1b35-56bd-b9aa-096c2d3b0e3c","330":"instance--e0483688-da10-5376-8cf2-050bcc3b70f0","60":"instance--1293d9cc-16b2-5c67-a453-bd144aab133a","90":"instance--2b43cd52-10db-5b15-8ad5-c4b59496528b"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--5","properties":[["name","Reuse harvested credentials to push payload onward"],["description","If credentials or CI tokens are harvested, they could be reused to push the same payload in other repositories, which in turn could enable a worm-like propagation as we've seen with previous attacks."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0001","technique":"T1078"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--35652c79-2c41-5d60-81ba-b5e47aa554bf","120":"instance--53906203-fffb-5af3-b112-44a9b4b49b8f","150":"instance--465fbc8a-7b4c-569f-be00-c0fbc137fcfc","180":"instance--a653c96b-3673-5dfa-968e-188fffe4cc04","210":"instance--6a344cf5-bd5c-52db-84f5-23c7701c7a5e","30":"instance--913561d1-b5f3-54d2-8272-159233dfde54","330":"instance--d59fe52d-c897-5f3a-919a-c2273cb8a8b3","60":"instance--f1fd6a3d-bb83-543d-a379-39d4632978f7","90":"instance--4cd6fce2-0d24-57f0-b161-12a867cd1100","branch:False":"instance--f7e897b3-3607-5ea5-8d15-5f83ba8a60da","branch:True":"instance--39b5ac19-b0dd-5674-a7d9-d75e659fe9ea"},"id":"condition","instance":"attack-condition--1","properties":[["description","The decoded PUA characters lead to a script that appears very similar to the Open VSX samples"]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--2ff8b105-17d8-5bc8-9736-a71ca9281068","120":"instance--fe9b11f7-9a07-51c8-93b2-02f34148833b","150":"instance--15f0676c-2f2f-58cf-99a3-b5eade2d286e","180":"instance--cdc5e3d9-a0b4-5995-98a3-d1a29532ffb1","210":"instance--75ed5df8-ff2f-5667-9748-b8587a1ee318","30":"instance--46009917-4258-54e5-9e91-c46c4a45d34d","330":"instance--54845373-a5f0-5af0-b348-5b0a3b4fbe67","60":"instance--f1f8d9a5-1f2a-55c4-af9a-f2629bc0827a","90":"instance--ddfb6e54-4af9-5771-910f-b4c7ba6e9860","branch:False":"instance--64607b7d-a4bd-56e7-9116-7bc21201c8bf","branch:True":"instance--f635d174-aa29-531f-b9c8-0cc481c6c1dd"},"id":"condition","instance":"attack-condition--2","properties":[["description","If credentials or CI tokens are harvested, they could be reused to push the same payload in other repositories, which in turn could enable a worm-like propagation as we've seen with previous attacks."]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--79135dd4-1ee4-5416-8f25-699a951afa80","120":"instance--3087ed8f-f52f-5bc8-8c62-f9ae3264725f","150":"instance--57ed80e6-51e6-50f7-aad0-39bb33df0261","180":"instance--c5faf3bc-2d22-54bc-898b-31882ba7c4a4","210":"instance--766332d8-d34d-5820-9442-c32dc1a417ad","240":"instance--bca47815-218d-563d-b96b-55ff17065443","270":"instance--7ff5ac74-4c1f-50b0-b02f-b897e172a434","30":"instance--cc8cae0a-dc95-5e3f-bdd0-23dd9cfca432","300":"instance--bdad0536-1d47-52b9-ab72-1c7a08158f20","330":"instance--16d7e8d9-53cf-5ae9-a219-2047733c1b5d","60":"instance--872a3352-ab12-5fc6-993d-6b22b7bc0454","90":"instance--e6a727e3-1e85-552c-b938-189e11fc5d41"},"id":"software","instance":"instance--763adce8-107c-58c1-9b65-18fefd501b17","properties":[["vendor","GitHub"],["evidence",[["item-1",{"excerpt":"the attacker seems to have turned their sights on GitHub","source":"https://www.aikido.dev/blog/the-return-of-the-invisible-threat-hidden-pua-unicode-hits-github-repositorties","source_field":"normalized_text"}]]],["display_name","GitHub"],["name","GitHub"],["diagram_instance","instance--763adce8-107c-58c1-9b65-18fefd501b17"]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--7bca99b4-fc37-5b67-9da4-7aaaaca1937e","120":"instance--a653e288-958c-5a34-826a-c7ae2da3173f","150":"instance--9fb91ed2-00e9-50c3-8ceb-3f10b07b73bc","180":"instance--bf4d856a-43b2-58e9-a272-467b1a321907","210":"instance--10ca6953-dd7d-54b7-9406-bb40125e27e2","240":"instance--db0c8479-7e26-5d86-b4d9-d52f19ad3f45","270":"instance--3f9b75b2-1c8a-564a-8a7b-b898a27995dd","30":"instance--3663489e-5635-5e70-b0e5-70a502523b87","300":"instance--bdba1e6c-e0e6-5e31-a7d0-c53e76e3cb8b","330":"instance--163f5749-44cf-50b1-ba73-97edab024b3b","60":"instance--7d417c1a-591b-5278-821e-7d21ac26d33f","90":"instance--4d5c0684-fd37-55f3-860f-2e9735603afe"},"id":"software","instance":"software--2","properties":[["vendor","Solana"],["evidence",[["item-1",{"excerpt":"The decoded script appears to use Solana as a delivery channel, fetching and executing a payload from the blockchain.","source":"https://www.aikido.dev/blog/the-return-of-the-invisible-threat-hidden-pua-unicode-hits-github-repositorties","source_field":"normalized_text"}]]],["display_name","Solana"],["name","Solana"]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--421df5c3-c06a-506c-b439-2f075a03f3ff","120":"instance--a01eea82-712a-5f6e-8f80-ac883be148c1","150":"instance--c4d026ee-cd8c-5d6e-816d-e432806e0984","180":"instance--554cb5af-dc83-5c2d-8f08-1080d97d0496","210":"instance--4251388c-a6e1-598c-b55e-9578d4bbfc0e","240":"instance--dfe9f92e-72d6-5f67-979a-96f743302fc4","270":"instance--c174391f-73ce-5882-b338-7dde16dc1955","30":"instance--477ac67f-63c3-5e61-8981-3efc5982ce01","300":"instance--c266e078-dcb0-5dce-8bdf-e2b3ba4a6251","330":"instance--